# Gentoo penguin

The gentoo penguin breeds on the Antarctic Peninsula and the subantarctic
islands, recognisable by the white band across the crown and the orange bill. It
takes krill, squid and small shoaling prey while submerged, beating its flippers
to propel itself through the water and turning on a wingtip, and is the fastest
of its family below the surface. Its descents are shallow beside those of its
larger relatives, most ending within thirty metres. The brood is raised on a
circular pile of pebbles, and a stolen pebble is a common cause of quarrel in a
colony. See [[spheniscidae]].
